  "translationRepairs": [
    ["s0021","idiomatic","The National History Institute now holds Chen Daren's Jin-dynasty \"Liao Ritual Treatise,\" which records their native customs, and also a \"Miscellaneous Liao Rites,\" largely in the Chinese style.","The National History Institute now holds a \"Liao Ritual Treatise\" by Chen Daren of the Jin dynasty, which records Liao native customs, and also a \"Miscellaneous Liao Rites,\" largely in the Chinese style.","金 identifies Chen Daren as a Jin-dynasty author. The revised wording preserves that relationship in natural English instead of the awkward possessive ‘Jin Chen Daren's.’","high","applied"],
    ["s0075","literal","Whoever hit the willow pledged goods against the marker of the willow's crown and robes; whoever missed pledged crown and robes as stake.","Whoever hit the willow took as pledge the crown and robes of the willow's marker; whoever missed pledged his own crown and robes.","中柳者質誌柳者冠服 means the hitter takes the willow-marker's crown and robes as pledge; the original literal reverses that direction, and the proposed wording matches 不中者以冠服質之 for the misser's own stake.","high","applied"]
  ],
